Note: the same upstream repository also contains an encoder (`libmpcenc`/`mpcenc`), which is
licensed LGPL-2.1-or-later. No encoder code was read for algorithmic understanding or ported into
this crate; `mpcenc` was only used, unmodified and unlinked, as an external, throwaway fixture
generator during development (to produce test `.mpc` files that were fed to the *decoder*
oracle), exactly like `ffmpeg` was used as a decode oracle. Its license has no bearing on this
crate's contents. FFmpeg's own (L)GPL-licensed mpc7/mpc8 decoders were never read.

# Convention for ported files

Every source file in this crate that ports algorithmic logic from `libmpcdec` carries a header
comment of the form:

    Ported from libmpcdec <path/to/file.c> (BSD-3-Clause), see NOTICE.

pointing back to this file. Files that only define Symphonia-specific glue (trait impls,
`FormatReader`/`AudioDecoder` registration, etc.) do not carry this notice.

# Specifications

The SV7 bitstream layout and the SV8 packet/chunk format are also documented independently by the
Musepack project at https://www.musepack.net/index.php?pg=src (SV8 specification and legacy SV7
notes); those specification documents were consulted alongside the reference decoder.
